<title>JAPAN: G7 forex statement &quot;getting through&quot;-Japan's Kato.</title>
<headline>G7 forex statement &quot;getting through&quot;-Japan's Kato.</headline>
<dateline>FUKUOKA, Japan 1997-05-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Takatoshi Kato said on Saturday a G-7 statement on foreign exchange stability was getting through to markets.</p>
<p>Asked by Reuters if he thought the G-7 statement was getting through to foreign exchange markets in view of the growing strength of the yen against the U.S. dollar, Kato replied: &quot;Yes, I think it is getting through considerably.&quot;</p>
</text>
